{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A man shall not take his father's wife.</b> This does not deal here with the prohibition of a father's wife, nor does it come to teach us that there is a mamzer from those liable to karet — for example, from a father's wife — and the same applies to the other forbidden relations that carry karet. Rather, it cites the first one in the section of forbidden relations that carry karet in the book of Leviticus. And it deals with his father's raped woman, as it juxtaposes to it: 'and the man who lay with her etc.' Therefore it was juxtaposed here." "<b>And he shall not uncover the corner of his father.</b> It is the corner that his father saw, in the manner of 'and you shall spread your corner over your handmaid.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:53.710540280Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}